{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0e75c6122e9494b0ab34b9fd39c54374007406a4e99b7707177fde2ce8f0aa59"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Vibra Code is an open-source AI app builder: users describe mobile apps in plain English, a backend runs Claude Code inside an E2B cloud sandbox to generate apps, and a live preview appears on the phone."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1d9380c1291c81122dadb9580c9a762d3e92d3f7676a016cd0c487d38887e7d7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The mobile app's core is a native iOS chat UI built with Texture (AsyncDisplayKit) and IGListKit, described as off-main-thread rendering targeting 60fps scrolling."},{"claim_ids":["clm_445804377daa31d0e9b21d2ebe36cd33324a0cf2295744c91f6c4b09e337bf3d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users can describe apps by voice or attach mockup screenshots as input, and generated projects can be pushed directly to GitHub."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5625c342cdfd7f6e6a0b8c3a6f3f1b6eb387742043d92186fde32e3de7859cc9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product supports multiple AI providers — Claude (default), Cursor, and Gemini — switchable with a single environment variable."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b91b195d318c0d2d0e68d8cac7582c16be658cfa2a30d697f1f39836965398d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The iOS client exposes modals for selecting the AI provider, browsing generated files, viewing live sandbox logs, publishing to GitHub, haptic settings, and editing environment variables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_734af18fee98c96bef519d6e82a00427728c9502813ab750ba1362b9f533cdb3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README positions Vibra Code as an open-source, self-hostable alternative to closed-source AI app builders such as Vibe Code App, Rork, Lovable, and Bolt.new, focused on native mobile apps built with Expo."},{"claim_ids":["clm_79062d92b4b0075f561ad1c80f8f1dd3a935486c9abb070efaf93bdcbdbae02a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented flow: the backend creates a Convex session, Inngest spawns an E2B sandbox where the AI agent generates code, updates stream back via Convex, and the phone opens a live preview through a tunnel URL."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c95997c3b33926e0be620488cf9839a1e86e92b65f9571b81c6a16982d43927e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Real-time synchronization is handled by Convex, with changes streaming from the sandbox to the phone instantly."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d0c23800c7a6a68117821473a482035ed58133629e9448735eb5c0bf7e4b53dd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Chat messages from Convex are rendered as distinct node types: text with markdown, file reads (blue), edits (orange), bash commands (green), todo task cards, and a working-status indicator."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d6d41f0cd3270c0f3df8d842973b47e73926df195c37e0635240ce3d1650bb02"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Required configuration includes ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for AI generation, E2B_API_KEY for sandboxes, Clerk keys for authentication, and a Convex deployment URL; Stripe and RevenueCat keys are optional, only for payments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_da348189e82c6d871ea166c3aeea220bba0ab26e0974ddd3ba249d3b87364a3a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture diagram shows three tiers: an Expo iOS app talking over an API to a Next.js + Convex server, which queues work via Inngest to an E2B sandbox running the AI agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e80fa95b83428210a0afb5e27216a39ef33389677390623f540b2ee6b8632af6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is licensed under AGPL-3.0 and is positioned as self-hostable with customizable AI prompts and swappable AI providers."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0e75c6122e9494b0ab34b9fd39c54374007406a4e99b7707177fde2ce8f0aa59","clm_1d9380c1291c81122dadb9580c9a762d3e92d3f7676a016cd0c487d38887e7d7","clm_445804377daa31d0e9b21d2ebe36cd33324a0cf2295744c91f6c4b09e337bf3d","clm_5625c342cdfd7f6e6a0b8c3a6f3f1b6eb387742043d92186fde32e3de7859cc9","clm_6b91b195d318c0d2d0e68d8cac7582c16be658cfa2a30d697f1f39836965398d","clm_734af18fee98c96bef519d6e82a00427728c9502813ab750ba1362b9f533cdb3","clm_79062d